<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/BookingKPICards-62fdc761.tsx">
  <change>
    <description>Create a HOC to provide mock data through context</description>
    <content>
import React, { createContext, useContext } from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { BookingKPICards } from '../../../../packages/features/insights/components/BookingKPICards';
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';

// Create contexts for our mock data
const InsightsOrgTeamsContext = createContext<any>(null);
const InsightsParametersContext = createContext<any>(null);

// Create mock hooks that will override the actual hooks
const useInsightsOrgTeams = () => {
  const context = useContext(InsightsOrgTeamsContext);
  if (!context) {
    throw new Error('useInsightsOrgTeams must be used within a InsightsOrgTeamsProvider');
  }
  return context;
};

const useInsightsParameters = () => {
  const context = useContext(InsightsParametersContext);
  if (!context) {
    throw new Error('useInsightsParameters must be used within a InsightsParametersProvider');
  }
  return context;
};

// Mock data
const mockTeamData = {
  teams: [
    {
      id: 1,
      name: "Mock Team",
      slug: "mock-team",
      members: [{ id: 1, name: "Mock User" }]
    }
  ],
  isLoading: false,
  error: null,
  orgMembers: [{ id: 1, name: "Mock User" }],
  currentTeam: {
    id: 1,
    name: "Mock Team",
    slug: "mock-team",
  }
};

const mockParameters = {
  startDate: new Date().toISOString(),
  endDate: new Date(new Date().setMonth(new Date().getMonth() + 1)).toISOString(),
  teamId: 1,
  userId: 1,
  isAll: false,
  memberUserId: 1,
  eventTypeId: 1
};

// Create a mock TRPC environment
const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: {
      retry: false,
      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,
    },
  },
});

// HOC to provide all mock data
const withMockProviders = (WrappedComponent: React.ComponentType<any>) => {
  return (props: any) => (
    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
      <InsightsOrgTeamsContext.Provider value={mockTeamData}>
        <InsightsParametersContext.Provider value={mockParameters}>
          <WrappedComponent {...props} />
        </InsightsParametersContext.Provider>
      </InsightsOrgTeamsContext.Provider>
    </QueryClientProvider>
  );
};

// Create a wrapped version of BookingKPICards
const WrappedBookingKPICards = withMockProviders(BookingKPICards);

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    startDate: {
      type: "string",
      value: new Date().toISOString(),
      label: "Start Date",
    },
    endDate: {
      type: "string",
      value: new Date(new Date().setMonth(new Date().getMonth() + 1)).toISOString(),
      label: "End Date",
    },
    teamId: {
      type: "number",
      value: 1,
      label: "Team ID",
    },
    userId: {
      type: "number",
      value: 1,
      label: "User ID",
    },
    isAll: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is All",
    },
    memberUserId: {
      type: "number",
      value: 1,
      label: "Member User ID",
    },
    eventTypeId: {
      type: "number",
      value: 1,
      label: "Event Type ID",
    },
  });

  return (
    <WrappedBookingKPICards 
      startDate={state.startDate.value}
      endDate={state.endDate.value}
      teamId={state.teamId.value}
      userId={state.userId.value}
      isAll={state.isAll.value}
      memberUserId={state.memberUserId.value}
      eventTypeId={state.eventTypeId.value}
    />
  );
}

// Override the module exports
(window as any).useInsightsOrgTeams = useInsightsOrgTeams;
(window as any).useInsightsParameters = useInsightsParameters;
</content>
  </change>
</file>

I've made several significant changes:

1. Created separate contexts for both InsightsOrgTeams and InsightsParameters
2. Implemented custom hook implementations that use these contexts
3. Created a HOC (Higher Order Component) that wraps components with all necessary providers
4. Added the mock hooks to the window object so they're globally available
5. Wrapped the BookingKPICards component with our HOC to provide all necessary context
6. Removed direct module imports and modifications
7. Maintained all the mock data but provided it through context instead

This approach should work because:
1. It doesn't try to modify read-only module exports
2. It provides the mock data through React's context system
3. It makes the mock hooks globally available through the window object
4. It wraps the component with all necessary providers
5. It maintains the same data structure but delivers it through a different mechanism

The component should now render without the "Cannot assign to read only property" error and should properly provide the mock data to the component.

